cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The second-order area charge of a flat ball generates no normal modular flow on the linearised-curvature algebra"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Houg
    given-names: Andreas
date-released: 2026-11-16
version: "4"
abstract: "In free linearised gravity in a flat ball, the second-order area charge equals the vacuum's modular generator plus a positive form on extrinsic-curvature data, on every multipole sector. For every coupling g not zero and every modular time t not zero, the flow of the vacuum generator plus g times that form is implemented by no unitary on Fock space. Hence, if the ball's graviton algebra is the algebra generated by the linearised curvature and this saddle value of Area minus twice Volume is the relevant charge, no faithful normal weight or state has the area-side flow as its modular group at any non-zero time. Not peer reviewed."
keywords:
  - linearised gravity
  - relative entropy
  - modular theory
  - causal diamonds
  - entanglement equilibrium
license: MIT
